  "government_note": "genitive on the complement is constant across every row; no row emits a case claim",
  "increment": "inc-preposition-sense-discriminators",
  "inventory_status": "teaching inventories (4/4/3/3 plus one contested row); the classical inventories are longer",
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "prp-r1",
      "text": "discriminator features are SUPPLIED evidence — the governing predicate's class, the complement's semantic type, and the outcome of the paraphrase test; the token alone never fixes the sense"
    },
    {
      "id": "prp-r2",
      "text": "the preposition's identity is itself a discriminator, so a sense row is only ever reachable for its own preposition; a missing preposition feature abstains"
    },
    {
      "id": "prp-r3",
      "text": "government is INVARIANT across senses: every preposition here assigns genitive whichever sense is selected, so a sense decision never touches the case and a case reading never selects a sense"
    },
    {
      "id": "prp-r4",
      "text": "the paraphrase test is required evidence where the row declares it; an unrun test is missing evidence and abstains rather than defaulting to the commonest sense"
    },
    {
      "id": "prp-r5",
      "text": "exactly one survivor -> that sense (candidate); more than one -> preserve_alternatives; none -> abstain insufficient_features. No preposition here has a default sense"
    },
    {
      "id": "prp-r6",
      "text": "the contested comitative-vs-transitivising reading is declared as TWO overlapping rows, so that environment preserves both readings instead of asserting the source's pick"
    },
    {
      "id": "prp-r7",
      "text": "the sense lists are the source's teaching inventories and are NOT the classical inventories, which are longer; a no-survivor outcome means unlisted here, never ill-formed"
    },
    {
      "id": "prp-r8",
      "text": "expletive occurrences and prepositions selected lexically by a particular verb are outside this table and are never forced into a compositional sense"
    }
  ],
